cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pyshiro-fast in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "pyshiro-fast: fast HSMM forced alignment for Japanese singing voice"
abstract: >-
  A drop-in fork of pyshiro with a rewritten Viterbi decoder for HSMM forced
  alignment. Duration-axis pruning, an O(1) sliding-window argmax in the
  duration-free pass, packed 32-bit backpointers and Hirschberg
  divide-and-conquer traceback make long-audio alignment 100-700x faster while
  producing bit-identical segments and log-likelihood.
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
repository-code: "https://github.com/henley04/pyshiro-fast"
url: "https://henley04.github.io/pyshiro-fast/"
keywords:
  - forced alignment
  - HSMM
  - singing voice
  - Japanese
  - lyrics
authors:
